{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1500103-christmas-spirits","id":1500103,"title":"Christmas Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-19T10:09:46-08:00","id":1500103,"title":"Christmas Spirits","content":"Yuletide is here and I'm likely to be busy with a sick little goblin at home, so posting my Christmas offerings now. Although I might have one more (plus some Monster Mash) before the month is up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>One Thousand Eyes</b><br /> Tree spirits, as a rule, are crotchety bastards and One Thousand Eyes has that character trait in spades. Cantankerous and resentful, Eyes jealously guards his neighborhood, challenging anyone, werewolf or spirit, encroaching its territory. As a spirit representing Christmas trees, however, One Thousand Eyes is only really active during the month of December, giving plenty of time for competing claims to the space to arise. Eyes hates the entire situation. It hates other spirits who see it as an upstart and an egomaniac. It hates werewolves for their holier than thou arrogance. And most of all, it hates the humans for giving it bountiful Essence for a single month, then nothing for the rest of the year.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One Thousand Eyes appears to be an extravagantly decorated Christmas tree at first glance. Closer inspection reveals that the lights gracing its boughs are actually shining eyeballs and its roots are hundreds of wooden arms and hands. Even at the best of times, the spirit comes across as indigent and sarcastic, although that quickly devolves into out-and-out venom and disdain. The only spirits One Thousand Eyes seems to genuinely fear are the Helions. Legend has it that the tree spirit somehow offended Helios himself and is waiting for the day the god\u2019s minions come to exact vengeance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>One Thousand Eyes</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Rank 3 Tree Spirit</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Attributes: </b>Power 7 Finesse 4 Resistance 9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Willpower:</b> 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Essence:</b> 20</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Initiative:</b> +13</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Defence:</b> 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Speed:</b> 18</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Size:</b> 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Corpus:</b> 16</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Influences: </b> Light \u2022, Trees \u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Numina:</b> Awe, Gift Giver, Dement, Drain, Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Discorporiation, Reaching, Shadow Gateway</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ban:</b> Cannot enter sunlight.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bane:</b> Fire fueled by gifts earnestly given that will be sorely missed.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>New Numen - Gift Giver: </i>By spending 5 Essence, One Thousand Eyes can rearrange a werewolf\u2019s Gifts. The werewolf temporarily loses access to one of their normal Gifts and gains the Gift of Insight, Inspiration, Nature, or Weather in its place with the same Facets unlocked. Alternatively, One Thousand Eyes can also use this Numen to temporarily swap the unlocked Facets of the aforementioned Gifts as long as the target meets the Renow requirements. Either way, the change lasts until the next moon rises. If used on an unwilling werewolf, this provokes a Clash of Wills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Creeping Frost</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Ice wants in. Ignore everything you know about Brownian motion and kinetic energy and look to the Shadow instead. Do you see them? The squirming icy bugs with human faces? The ones the size of cats, chewing at your house's insulation? That's the cold coming in, squirming its way through any crack or crevasse it can find. It is coming for you and if you aren't careful, it will kill you.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The <i>asde-skol</i> are ubiquitous in regions where the temperature regularly drops below freezing. They are liminal spirits, who feast on the resonance of dwindling warmth, frozen drafts, and failing insulation. They simply love humanity for building such nice warm larders for them to rip apart with their frozen mandibles. Even better, the flesh things restock and repair the spirit\u2019s playhouses after they break them open, starting the game anew. It doesn\u2019t bother the winter spirits that they rarely have the same human \u201cplaymates,\u201d there is always more flesh willing to move in, even after the last ones turned to ice. In the meanwhile, they can just move down the block to suck the warmth out of some other abode while the For Sale signs are up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Creeping Frost (Asde-Skol)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Rank 1 Winter Spirit</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Attributes: </b>Power 2 Finesse 2 Resistance 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Willpower:</b> 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Essence:</b> 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Initiative: </b>+4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Defense:</b> 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Speed: </b>9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Size:</b> 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Corpus: </b>4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Influences: </b>Cold \u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Numina:</b> Eutrophic Decay, Seek</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Reaching</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ban:</b> Do not rest where heat can find you.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bane: </b>Flame from a hearth.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Creeping Frost as a Totem</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The <i>asde-skol</i> are content enough spirits as long as can leech away heat and get their precious Essence. They stalk the Shadow in swarms, massive schools of icy bugs to protect them against larger predators. Once they have a werewolf pack backing them up, however, all that changes. <i>Asde-skol </i>totems insist on their packs clearing other winter spirits from the territory, especially their former swarm-mates. They take the concept very seriously, making them popular amongst the Hunters in Darkness. Other than keeping competition and larger spirits at bay, Creeping Frost aren\u2019t demanding totems, seeing themselves as one amongst many within the pack rather than its lord and master. They are well aware that the Pack bond is the only thing allowing them to be active year-round and that they are likely to be torn to shreds by the swarm if the pack ever abandons them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cost: </b>Packs seeking (or demanding) patronage from an <i>asde-skol</i> must invest 6 dots into the Totem Merit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Boon: </b>Gain 1 dot of the Hardy Merit (<b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>p. 47)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sample Aspirations:</b> Spread the cold whenever possible, attack other <i>asde-skol</i>, drive away a Rank 3 blizzard spirit, destroy the furnace in a specific building, break all the windows in a mall.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Creeping Frost as a Touchstone</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Some <i>asde-skol</i> fall into Winter Wolf\u2019s court, who sends them to act as guides for Storm Lords fresh from the First Change. These Creeping Frosts retain their bug-like bodies, but in place of human faces, they have white wolf heads. As liminal spirits representing the transition between hot and cold, Creeping Frosts often approach Edoloths, advising them on how to mediate between extreme positions. They also bond well with Irakka, having an appreciation for subtleness and skulking into warm places where no one expects the cold.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-19-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T13:04:39-08:00","id":1500126,"title":"","content":"Oooh, nice. <br /> <br /> And now, I\u2019m certain that this is a typo, but \u201cEutrophic Decay\u201d sounds like an awesome Numen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core